; The same seam on the F64 path. `60 000 000 / 97.3` is not an integer,
; so the whole table falls to the floating-point arithmetic of plan 03
; (`integral` is false for the table, not just for the one segment) — and
; that is the path the gate exists for.
;
; Plan 03, phase 2's own row: `:qpm 97.3` then `150` at `13q`, where tick
; 599 639 040 has to come back from its own seconds. 13q is 599 639 040
; and 26q is 1 199 278 080.
;
; The boundary seconds are NOT hand-writable here — they are whatever the
; documented op order produces — so the echo's `:start-sec` column is
; where they are pinned, and `times.sjon` asks about exactly those bit
; patterns and the ulp below each.
(timeline :title "seams-three-segment-f64" :length 8bar)

(tempo-point :at 0q :qpm 97.3)
(tempo-point :at 13q :qpm 150)
(tempo-point :at 26q :qpm 200)
(meter-point :at 0bar :sig [4 4])
